=begin pod

=TITLE App::GitManager

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    gitmanager status
    gitmanager status --repo=/path/to/repo
    gitmanager status --all --repo=/path/to/parent
    gitmanager status --json
    gitmanager status --verbose

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Phase 1 of App::GitManager implements read-only inspection of one Git
working tree. With C<--all>, it examines immediate subdirectories of
C<--repo> that contain a C<.git> entry (including linked worktrees).
It does not recursively descend into nested projects.

No network requests, fetches, pulls, pushes, staging, commits, resets,
branch deletion, or changes to tracked files occur.

Git's C<--no-optional-locks> option is used to prevent optional index
refresh writes during status inspection.

Ahead and behind counts compare HEAD to the cached upstream tracking
reference. They do not establish whether the GitHub server has newer
commits. An absent upstream produces unknown counts.

=head1 OPTIONS

=item C<--repo=PATH>       Repository path or parent directory for C<--all>.
=item C<--all>             Examine immediate repositories below the parent.
=item C<--remote=NAME>     Remote whose URL is displayed; default C<origin>.
=item C<--json>            Machine-readable status report.
=item C<--verbose>         Include branch lists.
=item C<--dry-run>         Accepted; this command is already read-only.
=item C<--yes>             Accepted; no confirmations needed for status.
=item C<--no-interactive>  Accepted; status never prompts.

=head1 EXIT CODES

0 for success, 1 when repositories cannot be inspected or none are found,
2 for unsupported options, commands, or invalid arguments.

=head1 ROADMAP

Future phases: sync, pr, prune-branches, and release. These commands
are intentionally NOT implemented in Phase 1.

=end pod
